# local env files
#
# R-10: this used to be `.env*.local` ONLY, so a bare `.env` — the single most
# likely place for a real key to sit — was NOT ignored and one `git add .`
# away from a PUBLIC repo. Cover every .env form and re-admit the committed
# template explicitly.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# netlify
.netlify

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
